---
const canonicalUrl = 'https://superada.ai/max-ai-vertical-ops-product-brief-v1/';
const names = [
  'FieldMax',
  'ServicePilot',
  'RepairDesk AI',
  'TradeOps Agent',
  'RouteReady',
  'JobBrain',
  'ApplianceOps',
  'CrewCopilot',
  'Dispatch Agent',
  'Max for Trades',
];
const nextSteps = [
  'Pick one starting vertical, with in-home appliance repair as the default because the warmest distribution signal is there.',
  'Ask the phone-service operator or adjacent connector for 3 to 5 warm intros, not market feedback in the abstract.',
  'Choose one operator workflow for the ugly MVP: next appointment, job lookup, parts-to-order, or follow-up reminder.',
  'Map the data surface for that workflow: scheduling, customer records, job notes, parts, phone or SMS history, and owner permissions.',
  'Build a narrow internal assistant first. It should help the technician or owner before any customer touches it.',
  'Run the pilot free for 60 to 90 days, then test a simple $100/month-ish price if the business keeps using it.',
  'Only after internal trust exists, expose the customer-facing layer over iMessage, WhatsApp, SMS, or web chat.',
  'Use the pilot to decide whether Max AI becomes B2B software, B2B2C network, or stays a vertical service business wedge.',
];
---
